    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="0d4a30b0-8331-5592-bb66-71bb292ae177" activityNameId="4062e930-2ed0-561e-aa69-ea8c3d4a4d8f" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Natural gas, production QA, at long-distance pipeline</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Natural gas, production QA, at long-distance pipeline
In 2023 0% of the imported Qatari natural gas to ES was imported by pipeline and 100% as LNG. An average distance of 0 km is estimated for the pipeline export from Qatar, of which are 0 km offshore pipeline. The estimated shipping distance for LNG are 8700 km. The net calorific value of natural is 36.0 MJ/Nm³. UUID=83b7ac70-709e-3037-8b2c-3fca78876d09
This dataset describes the transport needed for an average export of Qatari natural gas. Gas losses and emissions during seasonal storage are included.
Location: The data for storage emissions are based on global data. The amount of gas stored is a rough estimate based on European data. The average weighted transport distance is based on the trade movements 2019.
Technology: The distance is an European average based on the European long-distance pipeline network and LNG shipping routes.
Time period: Transport modes investigated for 2023.
Production volume: not known
Sampling: Literature.
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_83b7ac70-709e-3037-8b2c-3fca78876d09.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
